Attack 5 (desktop nav) — FAIL, in-scope regression
   Baseline (no Duplicates badge, current fixture data — UnresolvedDuplicateCount
   is 0 so the real badge never renders): branch nav at 1280 is one line,
   maxRight=1207.75 inside the 1280 container (72px headroom); this matches
   RF1 acceptance criterion 5 as literally tested and PASSES.

   BUT the attack-surface instruction explicitly requires simulating the
   Duplicates badge (a real, existing conditional block in base.html,
   `{{if .UnresolvedDuplicateCount}}`, unowned/untouched by RF1, that fires
   whenever a household has unresolved duplicate transactions — a normal
   production state, not a contrived one). Injecting the EXACT real anchor
   markup (`relative px-2 py-2 ... whitespace-nowrap ...` + the badge span,
   copied verbatim from the current base.html diff) into the Setup nav group
   at a 1280px viewport:
     - BRANCH (:8143, RF1's fix — px-2/gap-4/whitespace-nowrap, 17px root):
       `document.documentElement.scrollWidth` = 1349 at a 1280px viewport —
       a NEW 69px horizontal page overflow. `maxRight` of the last nav link
       = 1293.33, past the 1280 container edge.
     - MASTER (:8153, true `git checkout master -- web tailwind.config.js`,
       same injected badge with MASTER's own real classes — px-3/gap-6, no
       whitespace-nowrap, 16px root): `document.documentElement.scrollWidth`
       stays exactly 1280 — NO horizontal overflow. (Master instead lets the
       badge-bearing link's text wrap onto a second line — several links'
       `top`s become non-uniform, `offsetHeight` 56-57px — a pre-existing,
       out-of-scope ugliness, but it does not create page-level horizontal
       overflow.)
     - Isolating cause: re-running the branch injection WITHOUT
       `whitespace-nowrap` (branch's own px-2/gap-4 + 17px root, badge
       present) still overflows (`scrollWidth`=1316), just by a smaller
       margin and via 2-line wrap instead of a fully off-container link —
       i.e. the 17px root bump alone leaves too little headroom for a 9th
       nav item at 1280px, and RF1's own `whitespace-nowrap` fix (needed to
       stop the base-case 3-link wrap named in ruling RF-2026-09-07a) turns
       that shortfall into full horizontal page overflow instead of vertical
       wrap once a realistic 9th item (the badge) is present.
     - At 1440px the same injected badge fits on branch with margin
       (maxRight=1373.33 < 1440) — the regression is specific to the named
       1280px breakpoint.

   This is a NEW horizontal overflow (RF.0: "no NEW horizontal overflow" at
   1280px, one of the run's three mandated viewports) directly caused by
   RF1's own committed file (web/templates/layouts/base.html, in-manifest)
   interacting with RF1's own root-font change (styles.css, in-manifest), in
   a state reachable through an existing, unmodified feature (the Duplicates
   badge) that ruling RF-2026-09-07a itself named as the failure mode this
   task's nav fix exists to close ("wraps three desktop nav links at
   1280 px"). The fix closes it only for the fixture's current 8-link,
   no-badge state; a realistic 9th-item state reopens it as overflow rather
   than wrap. In scope: base.html and styles.css are both in RF1's manifest,
   and RF1 acceptance criterion 5 states unconditionally "the nav's right
   edge stays inside the container."

